          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        rules: {
          objective: 'In each deal the highest bidder becomes soloist and chooses trumps. The soloist aims to take at least the number of points bid (from tricks, declarations, and last trick). Opponents try to prevent the soloist from making the bid. Minimum bid is 60 points in multiples of five.',
          gameplay: 'After the deal there is one round of bidding (minimum 60, bids in multiples of five); the highest bidder is soloist and declares trump, then leads to the first trick. Play follows standard Tute rules: follow suit, head the trick or trump if unable to follow; soloist may declare king-horse (40 in trumps, 20 in other suits) after winning a trick. Soloist makes the contract if their total (card points, declarations, and 10 for last trick) equals or exceeds the bid.',
          keyRules: [
            'Subastado = auction for trump',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
